---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand } from '../lib/metadata.js';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';
const b = brand();
---
<Base title="About | NorthRay Software" description="About NorthRay Software." current="about/">
  <h1>About NorthRay Software</h1>
  <p class="lede">{b.developer} is an independent software project making creative applications, starting with writing and publishing.</p>
  <div style="max-width:720px">
    <p>It's built around a simple belief: good software should be accessible to everyone, not just those who can afford it.
      Financial circumstances shouldn't decide whether someone can create, learn or express themselves.</p>
    <p>So the aim is useful, dependable desktop software that people genuinely enjoy using: thoughtfully designed, reliable,
      and capable of standing alongside established commercial alternatives, without unnecessary complications, artificial restrictions or expensive subscriptions.</p>
    <blockquote class="pull">We would rather release one application we're proud of than ten that barely work.</blockquote>
    <p>The current application is <a href={`${base}writing-studio/`}>NorthRay Writing Studio</a>, a writing and publishing studio for authors.
      <a href={`${base}download/#launcher`}>NorthRay Launcher</a> installs and updates it, and the apps that follow.</p>
    <h2>Free by philosophy</h2>
    <p>Our aim is to make NorthRay applications free to use, without subscriptions, paywalls or deliberately restricted features.
      If a feature makes the software better, the intention is for everyone to benefit from it.</p>
    <p>{b.developer} isn't built around investors or growth targets. Development, distribution and maintenance do have real costs, so we'll explore
      sustainable ways of supporting the project, without compromising the accessibility of the core applications, and explain them openly.</p>
    <h2>Your work belongs to you</h2>
    <p>Wherever practical, the apps keep your work on your own computer, work offline, and import and export established formats.
      Your writing, artwork and projects belong to you, and you shouldn't feel trapped inside an app or dependent on a constant internet connection.</p>
    <h2>Growing at our own pace</h2>
    <p>Software development is an ongoing process and mistakes are inevitable; what matters is acknowledging them and improving.
      Feedback, ideas and constructive criticism are welcome: the people who use the software should help shape its future.
      We're starting small, and we're comfortable with that.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="cj-philip" class="relationship" aria-labelledby="rel-title">
    <h2 id="rel-title">{b.developer} and CJ Philip</h2>
    <p style="max-width:720px">CJ Philip is a Scottish author, artist and broadcaster, and a creative partner of {b.developer}; the two are
      separate identities. CJ Philip Community, with his own apps such as CJ Radio (the home of The CJ Philip Show), is an optional
      download inside NorthRay Launcher. His books, artwork and programmes are his own.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="kicker">Questions</p>
  <p><a href={`${base}contact/`}>Get in touch</a>.</p>
</Base>
